== Match report ==

=== Jarin 1–0 Jacan ===
[[Jarin national football team|Jarin]] had to wait until stoppage time to break down [[Jacan national football team|Jacan]] in [[Castramara]], but Petros Shimora's late winner made sure of the points. Jacan defended stubbornly for long stretches, yet Jarin kept pressing and finally found the decisive moment at the death.

Goalscorer: Petros Shimora (90+3')

=== Asikyira 1–0 Yanbaru ===
[[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] controlled much of the contest in [[Sanropura]] and were rewarded late when Amadou Baal scored the only goal of the match. [[Yanbaru national football team|Yanbaru]] stayed organised and limited clear chances, but the East Fosians eventually ran out of answers.

Goalscorer: Amadou Baal (75')

=== Burawa 4–0 Sinchew ===
[[Burawa national football team|Burawa]] were the most dominant side of the day in [[San Chorche]], racing into a two-goal lead through Petre Xirsi and Qaasim Dhaxol before finishing strongly after the break. Further goals from Yaxye Cumar and Xirsi Shire turned the match into a comfortable win over [[Sinchew national football team|Sinchew]].

Goalscorers: Petre Xirsi (18'), Qaasim Dhaxol (20'), Yaxye Cumar (49'), Xirsi Shire (56')

=== Varkana 3–1 Breisland ===
[[Varkana national football team|Varkana]] struck first in [[Telukuba]] through Hugo Loria and then pulled away after halftime with goals from Luka Paliashvili and Gigo Bugadze. [[Breisland national football team|Breisland]] grabbed a consolation goal late on, but the result had already been settled.

Goalscorers: Hugo Loria (34'), Luka Paliashvili (58'), Gigo Bugadze (79'); Breisland: Player A (6')

=== Orma 1–0 Potocsí ===
[[Orma national football team|Orma]] edged a tight match against [[Potocsí national football team|Potocsí]] in [[Pangkalsimpang]], with Mikael Dirra scoring the decisive goal in the second half. Potocsí remained competitive throughout, but Orma's defensive shape held firm once they went ahead.

Goalscorer: Mikael Dirra (37')

=== Aetolia 2–0 Louyan ===
[[Aetolia national football team|Aetolia]] made the most of their opportunities in [[Valparaíso]], scoring once in each half through Nikos Stavridis and Petros Kallis. [[Louyan national football team|Louyan]] were unable to mount a meaningful response, and Aetolia collected a deserved clean-sheet victory.

Goalscorers: Nikos Stavridis (16'), Petros Kallis (38')

== Summary ==

Matchday 4 produced 13 goals, with [[Burawa national football team|Burawa]]'s 4–0 win over [[Sinchew national football team|Sinchew]] standing out as the day's biggest margin and [[Varkana national football team|Varkana]]'s 3–1 victory over [[Breisland national football team|Breisland]] also impressing. [[Jarin national football team|Jarin]], [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]], [[Orma national football team|Orma]], and [[Aetolia national football team|Aetolia]] all collected important wins, keeping the group stage picture competitive.

